<atten3>
<ptxt>The reference pages for when the above codes are output apply only when they are output by the CAN gateway ECU (V bus No.2 monitoring ECU). If an ECU other than the CAN gateway ECU outputs the above codes, it is necessary to identify the malfunctioning area from "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting".</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If a communication stop or bus malfunction occurs in an ECU connected to V bus No.2, the CAN gateway ECU detects the malfunction and outputs a DTC.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2WD models equipped with neither pre-crash safety nor radar cruise control have no V bus No.2 configuration and no CAN gateway ECU wiring.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
